From: Aaron N <aaronna@valvesoftware.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: no firmware log stream without tracing, signal
 dropped reg events, u64 BSS flag cache

Three Steam Frame kernel fixes, carried as one:

1. Don't ask the firmware for its log stream unless it can be
   consumed. ath12k_qmi_wlanfw_wlan_ini_send() always set enable_fwlog,
   so the firmware sends DIAG events, up to hundreds per second, that
   ath12k_wmi_diag_event() only hands to a tracepoint. Without
   CONFIG_ATH12K_TRACING each one is received and dropped.
   enable_fwlog now follows CONFIG_ATH12K_TRACING.
2. Complete regd_update_completed on dropped reg events.
   ath12k_reg_chan_list_event() assigned pdev_idx only after
   ath12k_reg_validate_reg_info() returned VALID, so DROP and FALLBACK
   replies reached out: with pdev_idx still 255 and complete_all() was
   skipped. Every country command arms the completion first, so a
   dropped reply orphaned it and the next ath12k_regd_update() stalled
   for its 3 second timeout ("Timeout while waiting for regulatory
   update"). The phy id is now recorded as soon as the event parses,
   and the out: path checks it against num_radios.
3. Keep the cached BSS change mask as u64. mac80211 passes
   link_info_changed() a u64 mask, and ath12k caches it for links whose
   vdev does not exist yet, to replay once the vdev is assigned. A u32
   cache truncated flags above bit 31, such as BSS_CHANGED_TPE.

Squashed from the Steam Frame kernel's sm8650-7.2 branch, bodies
identical:
  4ed1ce3fa ath12k: don't send DIAG events if there is no sink
  9f9eb662a wifi: ath12k: complete regd_update_completed on dropped reg events
  a498f595a wifi: ath12k: use u64 for cached BSS change flags
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h |  2 +-
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c  |  2 +-
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c  | 12 +++++++++---
 3 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
index b8fc06825..d68b08556 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
@@ -292,7 +292,7 @@ struct ath12k_key_conf {
 struct ath12k_vif_cache {
 	struct ath12k_tx_conf tx_conf;
 	struct ath12k_key_conf key_conf;
-	u32 bss_conf_changed;
+	u64 bss_conf_changed;
 };
 
 struct ath12k_rekey_data {
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
index 8c7c1936f..7b1c46698 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
@@ -3777,7 +3777,7 @@ static int ath12k_qmi_wlanfw_wlan_ini_send(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 	int ret;
 
 	req.enable_fwlog_valid = true;
-	req.enable_fwlog = 1;
+	req.enable_fwlog = IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ATH12K_TRACING) ? 1 : 0;
 
 	ret = qmi_txn_init(&ab->qmi.handle, &txn,
 			   qmi_wlanfw_wlan_ini_resp_msg_v01_ei, &resp);
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
index 68f24c158..fb01e8e29 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
@@ -6993,6 +6993,11 @@ static int ath12k_reg_chan_list_event(struct ath12k_base *ab, struct sk_buff *sk
 		goto mem_free;
 	}
 
+	/* Assign before validation so DROP/FALLBACK exits still complete
+	 * the regd_update waiter.
+	 */
+	pdev_idx = reg_info->phy_id;
+
 	ret = ath12k_reg_validate_reg_info(ab, reg_info);
 	if (ret == ATH12K_REG_STATUS_FALLBACK) {
 		ath12k_warn(ab, "failed to validate reg info %d\n", ret);
@@ -7009,7 +7014,6 @@ static int ath12k_reg_chan_list_event(struct ath12k_base *ab, struct sk_buff *sk
 	}
 
 	/* free old reg_info if it exist */
-	pdev_idx = reg_info->phy_id;
 	if (ab->reg_info[pdev_idx]) {
 		ath12k_reg_reset_reg_info(ab->reg_info[pdev_idx]);
 		kfree(ab->reg_info[pdev_idx]);
@@ -7047,8 +7051,10 @@ static int ath12k_reg_chan_list_event(struct ath12k_base *ab, struct sk_buff *sk
 	WARN_ON(1);
 
 out:
-	/* In some error cases, even a valid pdev_idx might not be available */
-	if (pdev_idx != 255)
+	/* pdev_idx is unvalidated or still 255 if the
+	 * event never parsed
+	 */
+	if (pdev_idx < ab->num_radios)
 		ar = ab->pdevs[pdev_idx].ar;
 
 	/* During the boot-time update, 'ar' might not be allocated,
